      "text": "Three traditions — Judaism, Christianity, Islam — share a genealogy, define themselves\npartly against each other, and have profoundly shaped global history. The shared lineage\nis real but contested: each tradition reads the common heritage differently and claims\nto be the correct development or supersession of what came before."
